# src/apps/daemon/internal/analysis/diagnostics

## Purpose
Network diagnosis and analysis owner: censorship diagnosis, clean-IP probing, IP posture, CDN/anti-bot inspection, TLS/SNI/HTTP/throughput checks, and result interpretation.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `analysis` (rank 3; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (131): `anti_bot.go`, `anti_bot_test.go`, `artifact_admission_plan.go`, `asn_spoof_test.go`, `browser_proxy_handoff_plan.go`, `cdn_candidates.go`, `cdn_discovery.go`, `cdn_discovery_test.go`, `cdn_scan.go`, `cdn_scan_test.go`, `censorship_diagnosis.go`, `censorship_diagnosis_test.go` …

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `diagnostics`.
- Notable exported surface: `APITraceEndpoint`, `APITraceObservation`, `APITraceSchemaPlan`, `APITraceSchemaRequest`, `AnalyzeIPSecurity`, `AntiBotDetector`, `ArtifactAdmissionPlan`, `ArtifactAdmissionRequest`, `AttemptStage`, `BlockingChange` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/netpolicy`, `internal/foundation/resourcebudget`, `internal/native/bridge`, `internal/networking/proxyconfig`, `internal/networking/tlsdecoy`, `internal/protocols/arq`, `internal/protocols/tlsfragment`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/workflows/jobs`.

## Invariants
- `analysis` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
